Z||000000||neohio||11-23-2001||01:33 PM||||My car is making a noise and I was wondering if any of you can figure it out?? as it sits in the driveway, you can turn the steering just a little bit back and forth and it makes  banging noise in the front right side.front and bottom ball joints, sway bar bushings, shock, upper control arm bushing and bolt,tie rod end, rack and pinion w/inner tie rod end..could this possibly be the rack bushing?? any help would be appreciated!!<BR>84 Fiero||||reg||5
Z||000001||neohio||11-23-2001||01:34 PM||||duh! everything i listed in my topic is brand new!!!||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||11-23-2001||06:36 PM||||Could be a bushing... before you mess with the rack...<P>check the U joints in the steering column. one is under the dash and the other is down by the rack. Make sure both joints are good and the pinch bolts are tight.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Eriamjh||11-24-2001||12:54 PM||||Did you check to see that all the lug nuts are tight?<P>Is the caliper on tight?||||reg||1
